# What `railway up` must not ship.
#
# `railway up` uploads the working directory, not the git tree, so
# .gitignore is not automatically the whole story. target/ is around
# 6 GB of Rust build artifacts — none of it is needed, because the
# Dockerfile compiles from source inside the image, and trying to carry
# it is what makes a deploy fail with:
#
#   Repository snapshot operation timed out. This may be due to a large
#   repository size or network issues.
#
# Keep this in step with .dockerignore. The two answer different
# questions — what gets uploaded, and what the build context contains —
# but target/ is wrong in both.
target/
.git/

# Local only. The database URL and the seed admin password live here in
# development; on Railway they are service variables.
.env

# The compose stack and its init SQL are for a laptop, not the platform.
docker/
docker-compose.yml
